Z||000000||Philphine||09-03-2000||11:43 PM||||<BR>i recently mentioned a fiero i got for $125 off a thrift store donation lot. thats the least i've ever paid for a car. i've kind of decided to see how cheaply i can get it driveable. by that i mean have it be serviceable and not including things like stereos and paint jobs ( body is in really good shape but paint totaly faded). actually everything works but the stereo (and i'd change it anyway if i keep it), one head light motor (light itself works), one really deformed tire, and the engine itself.<P>so far i've changed the battery and cables (to top mount since i needed a new battery), gas tank and fuel pump with little success. i know they were bad so even if i don't have it figured out yet thats two things out of the way. i'll probaly check out the fuel injector next. i've doubled the original cost but still feel pretty good about the project. plus i hope i'm learning some stuff i can use later.<P>------------------<BR>Phil T<P>'87 coupe (feral)<BR>'84 indy<BR>'84 coupe||||reg||1
